.TH "PROBE::SCSI\&.IOEXEC" "3stap" "September 2026" "SystemTap Tapset Reference Ver" "SCSI Tapset"
.\" -----------------------------------------------------------------
.\" * Define some portability stuff
.\" -----------------------------------------------------------------
.\" ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
.\" http://bugs.debian.org/507673
.\" http://lists.gnu.org/archive/html/groff/2009-02/msg00013.html
.\" ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el       .ds Aq '
.\" -----------------------------------------------------------------
.\" * set default formatting
.\" -----------------------------------------------------------------
.\" disable hyphenation
.nh
.\" disable justification (adjust text to left margin only)
.ad l
.\" -----------------------------------------------------------------
.\" * MAIN CONTENT STARTS HERE *
.\" -----------------------------------------------------------------
.SH "NAME"
probe::scsi.ioexecute \- Create mid\-layer SCSI request and wait for the result
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.nf
probe scsi\&.ioexecute {}
.fi
.SH "VALUES"
.PP
\fIdata_direction\fR
.RS 4
The data_direction specifies whether this command is from/to the device\&.
.RE
.PP
\fItimeout\fR
.RS 4
Request timeout in seconds
.RE
.PP
\fIdevice_state\fR
.RS 4
The current state of the device
.RE
.PP
\fIlun\fR
.RS 4
The lun number
.RE
.PP
\fIchannel\fR
.RS 4
The channel number
.RE
.PP
\fIretries\fR
.RS 4
Number of times to retry request
.RE
.PP
\fIhost_no\fR
.RS 4
The host number
.RE
.PP
\fIrequest_bufflen\fR
.RS 4
The data buffer buffer length
.RE
.PP
\fIrequest_buffer\fR
.RS 4
The data buffer address
.RE
.PP
\fIdata_direction_str\fR
.RS 4
Data direction, as a string
.RE
.PP
\fIdevice_state_str\fR
.RS 4
The current state of the device, as a string
.RE
.PP
\fIdev_id\fR
.RS 4
The scsi device id
.RE
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
Prefer modern scsi_execute_cmd, but keep __scsi_execute / scsi_execute so RHEL8\-era 4\&.18 still resolves (scsi_execute was often only a macro around __scsi_execute)\&. 994724e6b3f0 introduced scsi_execute_cmd (opf / ml_retries instead of data_direction / retries)\&.
.SH SEE ALSO\n 
.IR tapset::scsi (3stap)
